#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""gentts - generate TTS audio from Markdown files.

Reads Markdown, strips everything unspeakable, converts structure into pause
markers, renders those markers for the chosen TTS provider, synthesises in
chunks and concatenates to a single MP3.

Per-file settings come from YAML frontmatter; CLI flags override frontmatter.

  gentts essay.md                       # -> essay.mp3
  gentts -l chapters/                   # list files and audio status
  gentts --preview essay.md             # show processed text, no API call
  gentts --dump-text essay.txt essay.md # write spoken text to file, no API call
  gentts -p openai -O out/ chapters/    # batch, OpenAI voice, into out/
  gentts --stamp essay.md               # write audio.file/duration back
  gentts -T essay.md                    # give the MP3 the .md's mtime

Frontmatter (all optional):

  ---
  title: In Search of Dharma
  subtitle: A natural history of ethics
  author: Biksu Okusi
  date: 2026-08-01
  language: en
  audio:
    title: "0: Preface"       # spoken title/subtitle/author/date, if
    subtitle: ...             #   they differ from the document's
    strip_h1: true            # drop a leading H1 the preamble already says
    provider: google          # google | openai | grok | compatible
    voice: en-AU-Chirp3-HD-Charon
    gender: male              # male | female (picks voice from the table)
    lang_code: en-AU
    output: ../html/audio/dharma.mp3
    lexicon: ./book_lexicon.json
    speaking_rate: 0.95
    preamble: true            # speak title/subtitle/author/date first
    skip: false               # exclude this file from batch runs
    timestamp: false          # give the MP3 the Markdown file's mtime
    markers: punctuation      # punctuation | tags (non-SSML providers)
    url: ...                  # 'compatible' provider only
    model: ...
    key_env: ...
    chunk_limit: ...

Inline fences in the body:

  <!--audio stop-->  ... excluded ...  <!--audio restart-->

Requires: python3.12+, PyYAML, ffmpeg, ffprobe; gcloud ADC for the Google
provider (gcloud auth application-default login).
"""

